---
import ArticleLayout from '../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import InShort from '../../../components/article/InShort.astro';
import ZenTip from '../../../components/article/ZenTip.astro';
import ZenPicture from '../../../components/article/ZenPicture.astro';

const checks = [
  { name: 'Your goal', record: 'Daily stress context, workout recovery or sleep patterns.', why: 'A training tool and a stress timeline may answer different questions.' },
  { name: 'Setup', record: 'App version, iPhone and Watch version, and the permissions you gave.', why: 'Features and available data can depend on your setup.' },
  { name: 'Data freshness', record: 'Time of the latest real reading, and the period the screen sums up.', why: 'A screen that just refreshed isn\'t always showing a new reading.' },
  { name: 'Missing data', record: 'Whether the app points out missing readings and explains them.', why: 'Missing data shouldn\'t be read as a low measurement.' },
  { name: 'Explanation', record: 'Named inputs, how the baseline works, and what the score means.', why: 'A number is more useful when you can see what it\'s based on.' },
  { name: 'Daily context', record: 'Whether the view tells apart exercise, rest and your own notes.', why: 'How you feel and a model\'s reading of your data are different records.' },
  { name: 'Access and cost', record: 'Required plan, local price, trial eligibility and renewal period.', why: 'Free to download doesn\'t mean the analysis is free.' },
  { name: 'Data controls', record: 'Where to review permissions, privacy information and deletion options.', why: 'Understand your choices before you share health data.' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout title="Apple Watch Stress App Comparison Worksheet: 8 Checks" description="Compare Apple Watch stress apps using eight practical checks: data freshness, missing readings, explanations, subscriptions and privacy. Download the free worksheet." published="2026-09-17" updated="2026-11-12">
<InShort image="/app-ui/start/zen_watch.webp" points={[
  'Judge apps by what you <strong>can check</strong>, not the nicest score.',
  'Record <strong>the same day</strong> in each app with eight simple checks.',
  'This is a worksheet, <strong>not an accuracy test</strong> or a ranking.',
]} />

<p><strong>Compare stress apps by what you can check, not by which one gives the best-looking score.</strong></p>
<p>Use this eight-check worksheet to record the same day in each app. Then pick the one that best answers your question.</p>
<p>This is a review tool written by Cortisol+. It is not a clinical accuracy test or a finished test of competitors.</p>
<p><a href="/downloads/apple-watch-app-checklist.csv" download>Download the blank comparison worksheet (CSV)</a>. Open it in Numbers, Excel or Google Sheets.</p>
<p>There's no signup, and the download doesn't send your answers to us.</p>

<h2>What should I compare?</h2>
<p><strong>Eight checks for an Apple Watch stress app.</strong> For each one, write down what you see.</p>
<ol class="not-prose my-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2" aria-label="Eight checks for an Apple Watch stress app">
  {checks.map((check, i) => (
    <li class="rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4">
      <p class="font-extrabold text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">{i + 1}. {check.name}</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink)]"><strong>Record:</strong> {check.record}</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-muted)]"><strong>Why:</strong> {check.why}</p>
    </li>
  ))}
</ol>

<ZenTip image="/app-ui/zen_new_tour_now.webp">
  Open every app at <strong>about the same time</strong> on the same day. Then you're comparing like with like.
</ZenTip>

<h2>How do I run a fair comparison?</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Pick one question and one date before you open the apps.</li>
  <li>Use the same device and similar time windows. Write down any differences instead of hiding them.</li>
  <li>Mark each check as <strong>observed</strong>, <strong>unclear</strong> or <strong>unavailable</strong>. Don't count an unknown as a failed feature.</li>
  <li>Keep screenshots private if they show personal readings. Note the page or screen behind each observation.</li>
  <li>Choose based on your own needs. Don't average scores from different apps, or call the highest score the most accurate.</li>
</ol>

<h2>What does an explanation look like in Cortisol+?</h2>
<figure><img src="/screenshots/wearable-insights.webp" alt="Cortisol+ Insights product example showing the cortisol, sleep and recovery inputs behind a wellness score" width="645" height="1398" loading="lazy" class="max-w-[280px] mx-auto rounded-2xl"/><figcaption>Existing Cortisol+ product example, not a participant result or competitor test. Use the input view for check 5 and inspect timestamps separately for check 3.</figcaption></figure>
<p>Read <a href="/how-it-works/">our score inputs and limitations</a>. You can also watch the <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">captioned development-build walkthrough with labeled sample data</a>.</p>
<p>These explain our product. They don't prove it's accurate against hormone tests.</p>

<h2 id="afib-history">Should I enable AFib History just to get more HRV readings?</h2>
<p><strong>No. Don't turn it on just to give a wellness app more data.</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-lamr/108375">Apple requires a doctor's diagnosis of atrial fibrillation (AFib) for AFib History</a>. It is not a general stress-tracking setting.</p>
<p>Use the features that fit your medical situation, and record the data your Watch actually gives you.</p>
<p>This checklist doesn't need you to change this setting. More readings alone wouldn't show that an app measures cortisol or reads your stress accurately.</p>

